From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 22:52:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: keep RD03v2 basic station statistics by default

qca-nss-pbuf controls ath11k statistics before it exits on host Wi-Fi. The
unset option defaults to one and sends a zero monitor filter and PPDU mask
after the 2.4 GHz AP starts. This produces zero signal, an empty average
and missing TX statistics; a later 5 GHz start masks the problem there.

With stats_disable=0 set before the radios start, the statistics are real
again, with extended counters off. Default to zero on this board, preserving explicit
configuration and the default for other boards. Buffer sizes are unchanged.
---
--- a/package/kernel/mac80211/files/qca-nss-pbuf.init
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/files/qca-nss-pbuf.init
@@ -211,9 +211,14 @@
 
 set_stats_disable() {
 
-  local stats_disable
+  local stats_disable stats_disable_default=1
+  # Basic RSSI and TX telemetry need the monitor/PPDU path. The legacy
+  # default clears that path after the first RD03v2 radio has started.
+  # Keep explicit disablement and other boards' defaults unchanged.
+  [ "$(cat /tmp/sysinfo/board_name 2> /dev/null)" = xiaomi,mi-router-ax3000t-v2 ] &&
+    stats_disable_default=0
   config_load pbuf
-  config_get stats_disable opt stats_disable 1
+  config_get stats_disable opt stats_disable "$stats_disable_default"
 
   [ -d /sys/kernel/debug/ath11k ] || return 0
 
